      "text": "First, we need to determine how many US dollars the painting costs in Namibian dollars. Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars, we divide the cost of the painting in Namibian dollars by 7:\n\n\\[ \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105 \\text{ Namibian dollars}}{7 \\text{ Namibian dollars/US dollar}} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert this amount from US dollars to Chinese yuan. Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan, we multiply the cost in US dollars by 6:\n\n\\[ \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan/US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan} \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
