    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan, we need to convert the cost from Namibian dollars to US dollars and then from US dollars to Chinese yuan.\n\n1. **Convert the cost from Namibian dollars to US dollars:**\n   The painting costs 105 Namibian dollars. Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars, we can find the cost in US dollars by dividing the cost in Namibian dollars by the exchange rate:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{105 \\text{ Namibian dollars}}{7 \\text{ Namibian dollars per US dollar}} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert the cost from US dollars to Chinese yuan:**\n   Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan, we can find the cost in Chinese yuan by multiplying the cost in US dollars by the conversion rate:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan per US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
