    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "1. First, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars. \n    - We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. \n    - The cost of the painting is 105 Namibian dollars. \n    - To find out how many US dollars this is, we use the conversion rate: \n    \\[\n    \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{\\text{Conversion rate}} = \\frac{105}{7}\n    \\]\n    - Calculating the above, we get:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Cost in US dollars} = 15\n    \\]\n\n2. Next, we need to convert the cost of the painting from US dollars to Chinese yuan.\n    - We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan.\n    - The cost of the painting is now 15 US dollars.\n    - To find out how many Chinese yuan this is, we use the conversion rate:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = \\text{Cost in US dollars} \\times \\text{Conversion rate} = 15 \\times 6\n    \\]\n    - Calculating the above, we get:\n    \\[\n    \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 90\n    \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
